            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "## Comment le mesure-t-on ?",
            "start": 232,
            "end": 259
          },
          {
            "id": "p5",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "On ne peut pas mesurer directement la taille d'un seul atome isolé (les électrons n'ont pas de \"bord\" net). Alors les scientifiques utilisent une astuce :",
            "start": 261,
            "end": 415
          },
          {
            "id": "p6",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. On mesure la distance entre les noyaux de deux atomes identiques liés par une liaison covalente",
            "start": 417,
            "end": 515
          },
          {
            "id": "p7",
            "category": "PROCEDURE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. On divise cette distance par 2",
            "start": 516,
            "end": 549
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The explanation correctly identifies the lack of sharp electron boundaries in isolated atoms and accurately states the standard operational definition of homonuclear covalent radius.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
